# Networking Rule

- Treat every network and IPC boundary as a trust boundary.
- Validate framing, message type, version, length, and semantic constraints before processing payloads.
- Use explicit timeouts and cancellation for network operations.
- Define bounded retry behavior; do not create unbounded retry loops.
- Handle disconnects, partial reads/writes, malformed messages, and peer shutdown deterministically.
- Preserve protocol compatibility and document intentional protocol changes.
- Avoid blocking I/O on hot paths.
- Keep connection lifecycle and resource ownership explicit.
- Add negative and integration tests for malformed input, timeouts, cancellation, reconnect, and protocol errors where applicable.
